"""Authored code-focus selections: exact source line and its semantic explanation."""
FOCUS={
1:('const int total',5,['const makes total read-only after initialization. int is the whole-number type. The + expression adds 7 and 5 at execution; = initializes the named result to 12. The compiler checks the types and may precompute this constant expression.','std:: names the standard-library namespace. ostringstream is an output stream that collects formatted text in an owned string rather than writing it immediately to a terminal.','For streams, << inserts the value on its right into the stream on its left. The quoted label is text; total supplies the number to format.','message.str() returns the collected text. std::cout sends it to standard output, and the character literal \\n supplies a newline. The operating system handles the underlying output service.','assert checks a Boolean condition during this verification build and stops the program if it is false. It does not prove the program correct for inputs the test never tried.']),
2:('auto copy',5,['auto asks the compiler to infer the type. No & appears, so copy is a separate vector with separate element storage.','auto& creates a reference: borrowed is another name for readings, not a second vector.','The [0] subscript selects the first element. Changing copy does not change readings.','The [1] subscript selects the second element. Writing through borrowed changes readings because both names reach the same vector.','The colon in this range-based for means take each element from readings in order. const int value makes a read-only value copy for that iteration; it is not a reference because there is no &. The stream prints each value followed by a space.']),
3:('const unsigned mask',2,['0xF is hexadecimal 15: four one-bits. The u suffix selects an unsigned type. << 4 shifts that group four positions to select bits 4 through 7.','~ flips the mask bits. & clears the selected old field; << positions the new field; | combines the non-overlapping groups. The old A field becomes 3 while the low 5 remains.']),
4:('const bool fits',1,['bool stores true or false. || evaluates its right side only if the left side is false. width == 0 avoids dividing by zero; otherwise count <= limit / width checks the bound without first forming a possibly overflowing product.']),
5:('const double large',2,['This constant is 2 to the power 53. The preceding static_assert lines require the floating-point representation used by this demonstration at compile time.','At this magnitude, binary64 cannot represent every consecutive integer. Under the default round-to-nearest environment, adding one rounds back to large. Floating-point addition is not exact real-number addition.']),
6:('const int* first',3,['const int* means a pointer through which the integers cannot be changed. The array expression supplies a pointer to its first element.','Adding two advances by two int elements, not two bytes. third points at the live third element of the same array.','Unary * reads the pointed-to integer. Subtracting pointers within this array counts elements, producing 2. The stream therefore prints 30 followed by 2.']),
7:('while (cursor',4,['The condition checks that cursor has not reached the legal one-past end marker. That marker may be compared but not dereferenced.','Unary * reads the current live element; += adds it to total. This read is safe because the loop checked the boundary first.','Prefix ++ advances to the next element, eventually reaching end. Without progress the loop would never finish.','The closing brace ends the loop body. Control returns to the condition before another element is read.']),
8:('auto temporary',3,['make_unique allocates and constructs one int with value 42. temporary is its sole owning handle; destruction of that owner would normally destroy the integer.','std::move permits the move assignment. unique_ptr transfers its ownership to owner and empties temporary; the integer itself stays alive at the same address.','The ! expression tests that the moved-from unique_ptr is empty. This empty-state guarantee is specific to unique_ptr; do not assume every moved-from type is empty.']),
9:('values.reserve',4,['reserve asks for storage capacity; it does not create an element or change size. A later growth may allocate a different buffer.','push_back constructs a new element at the end. The first live value is 4.','The second append may grow storage and invalidate previously borrowed element addresses. No such addresses are retained here.','The third append grows the live sequence to three elements. The vector owns and eventually destroys all three.']),
10:('const std::size_t start',4,['For these small fixture values, adding seven then dividing and multiplying by eight rounds the offset up to an eight-byte boundary. The generalized lab avoids overflow in this calculation.','&& requires both bounds. The subtraction is safe only after start <= capacity succeeds; request must fit in the remaining space.','The stream prints the aligned starting offset, not a real allocated address.','used advances past the requested bytes. Alignment padding also counts against the arena capacity. No C++ object lifetime starts in this offset-only model.']),
11:('try {',5,['try marks operations whose exceptions will be handled by the following catch.','at(3) requests the fourth element of a three-element vector. at checks bounds and throws before returning a value, so this line prints no number.','catch binds an exception of type out_of_range by const reference. It handles the bounds failure without copying or changing the exception.','The handler prints out of range. This is a defined failure path, unlike an unchecked invalid subscript.','The handler ends and execution continues after the try/catch statement.']),
12:('accumulator = operands',2,['pc++ supplies the current index and then advances pc. The first model instruction loads operands[0], so accumulator becomes 4 and pc becomes 1.','The next model instruction adds operands[1], making accumulator 7 and pc 2. These C++ statements model instruction effects; they do not dictate the compiler’s machine instructions.']),
13:('const std::uint64_t after_eax',2,['Converting the unsigned 32-bit value 7 to 64 bits gives 7 with zero high bits. This models the high-half clearing caused by an x86 EAX write.','The mask clears only the low sixteen bits before inserting 7. The other bits of old remain, modeling an AX write. ULL supplies a sufficiently wide unsigned literal.']),
14:('const auto address',1,['Multiplication is evaluated before addition: 3×4 produces byte offset 12; base 1000 and displacement 8 yield 1020. This is integer address arithmetic in a model, not permission to dereference address 1020.']),
15:('const int quotient',3,['Signed integer division truncates toward zero, so -17 / 5 is -3. Division by zero and the unrepresentable minimum-integer / -1 case must be rejected in a general function.','% computes the remainder belonging to that quotient. Here -17 = (-3)×5 + (-2), so the remainder is -2.','The stream prints quotient and remainder in that order. Neither is a rounded floating-point estimate.']),
16:('while (i <',4,['The branch allows iterations only for i equal to 0, 1, 2, and 3. At each loop entry, sum equals the total of all integers already passed.','Add the current i to the accumulated total. += changes the existing sum.','Incrementing i preserves the loop invariant for the next iteration and moves toward termination.','The body ends; test i < 4 again. When i reaches 4, control skips the body and sum remains 6.']),
17:('const auto helper',3,['[] introduces a lambda, an unnamed function object. Its empty capture list means it borrows no surrounding local variables. It accepts one int and returns twice that value.','saved names a value the caller still needs after the helper operation. const forbids changing it through this name.','Calling helper(3) yields 6. The compiler may inline the lambda or fold this calculation, so a C++ call expression does not prove that a machine call instruction exists.']),
18:('const int remembered',3,['remembered is a value copy of b, so it preserves the old value 4.','a refers to x. This write changes x to 9 and therefore changes what a later read through b sees.','b also refers to x, so this later read yields 9. Reusing remembered here would violate the required order when arguments alias.']),
19:('const auto kernel_copy',3,['This lambda accepts a requested length using size_t, the unsigned type for object sizes. It is only a model of a protection boundary.','The ?: conditional expression selects accepted when length is at most eight and rejected otherwise. Real kernel validation also depends on address range, access rights, and lifetime.','The lambda definition ends. Defining a function does not execute its body; the later two calls exercise different requests.']),
20:('if (!present)',4,['The model enters fault handling when the page is absent, counts one fault, and makes the page present. pc stays 8 during this recovery.','The assertion checks the condition required before the modeled load can complete.','The resumed load produces the fixture value 42. No actual page fault or memory mapping is created by this C++ program.','Only after completing the instruction does pc advance to 9. A denied fault would require a different outcome, covered by the lab.']),
21:('a = "waiting"',4,['A blocks for an event and becomes waiting. A waiting process cannot use a CPU merely because one becomes free.','B was ready and now becomes running. The model has moved the CPU to runnable work.','The first report shows A waiting and B running. These are string states, not real scheduler operations.','A becomes ready when its event arrives. It can now compete for a CPU, but it does not automatically displace B.']),
22:('process_a.at',3,['at looks up a key and returns access to its mapped value. Updating A’s map at numeric address 0x1000 changes only A’s stored value.','B uses the same numeric key in a different map, so the two reads print 11 and 9. Address-space identity is part of the translation context.','The assertion verifies B’s independent value. Shared memory would require a shared backing object, introduced in the extension lab.']),
23:('const unsigned page =',4,['Integer division by 4096 selects the virtual page number, here 1.','The remainder selects the unchanged within-page offset, here 564.','The fixture chooses frame 7 as the translation result. A real mapping lookup must also validate presence and permissions.','Recombine the chosen frame base with the original offset. This gives 7×4096+564 = 29236.']),
24:('const auto allowed',3,['[&] captures surrounding local objects by reference. The lambda accepts a Boolean indicating whether the requested access is a write.','Presence alone is insufficient. && also requires the permission selected by write ? writable : readable. A read is allowed here; a write is denied.','The callable is defined but has not yet checked an access. The calls below test both paths.']),
25:('if (!tlb_has_mapping)',5,['A missing cached translation triggers the modeled table walk. This says nothing yet about whether the data bytes are cached.','Increment the walk count for this translation lookup.','The fixture requires the page to exist in the page table. A missing page would follow a fault path instead.','Remember the successful translation in the TLB model. Later accesses could use it until invalidation or eviction.','The translation-miss path ends. The separate data_cached flag still determines whether the data lookup hits.']),
26:('if (!child.unique())',3,['If another owner shares the integer, allocate a new integer initialized from the old one and make child own it. This single-threaded decision is not a concurrent ownership protocol.','Dereferencing child now reaches the private integer, so writing 9 leaves parent’s integer unchanged.','The two reads print 7 and 9. Copy-on-write delays separation until a writer needs independent state.']),
27:('const auto time',2,['The lambda borrows latency and bytes_per_us. Transfer time is startup latency plus byte count divided by throughput; all terms must use compatible units.','The two calls produce 11 and 110 microseconds. Small transfers are dominated by startup cost; large ones by transfer cost. This model assumes no overlap.']),
28:('const int index',3,['The conditional chooses row-major visitation or column-major visitation of the same flat array. Both visit all sixteen logical elements.','Dividing by four groups four consecutive elements into one modeled cache block.','If the block differs from the sole resident block, count a miss and replace the resident. This deliberately tiny model isolates locality, not real CPU timings.']),
29:('const unsigned block',4,['Dividing the byte address by sixteen removes the within-block offset.','Remainder modulo four chooses one of four sets. Different block numbers can compete for the same set.','Dividing the block number by four supplies the tag that distinguishes those competing blocks.','The report exposes both set and tag. Matching a set alone does not establish a cache hit.']),
30:('const bool hit',4,['The slot holds a complete block number in this small model. Equality means the requested block is already resident; -1 represents an empty slot.','Adding a Boolean adds one for true and zero for false. hits records observed hits before any replacement.','Install the requested block even on a miss. This can evict another block mapped to the same slot.','Print H for the previously observed hit, M otherwise. Testing after installation would falsely turn every access into a hit.']),
31:('lru.erase',4,['The initial order is oldest to newest, A then B. Erasing the front removes A from its old recency position.','Touching A appends it as most recently used, giving B then A.','front now selects B as the least recently used victim.','FIFO still selects A because its arrival order has not changed. A hit must not silently change the selected policy into LRU.']),
32:('const double amat',2,['Average memory access time pays hit_time on every access and the additional miss penalty only on the miss fraction. Here 1 + 0.05×40 gives 3 nanoseconds.','The output includes units. This is an average-cost model; it is not a measured latency distribution or a guarantee for any one access.']),
33:('assert(offset <=',2,['Check the starting position first, then subtract it from the size. Short-circuit && prevents an unsigned subtraction underflow from being used as a false large capacity.','substr extracts three characters starting at offset two, giving CDE. Strings can represent byte ranges; the operation does not infer application record boundaries.']),
34:('const auto count',4,['min chooses the smaller of the fixture’s two-byte transfer limit and the remaining bytes. The last transfer will contain just one byte.','Append only the bytes actually transferred, beginning at the current position.','Advance by the actual count, not by the desired buffer size. This keeps the next operation at the first untransferred byte.','Count the completed modeled transfer. Five bytes at at most two per call require three calls.']),
35:('pending += "AB"',5,['The first two bytes enter the local pending buffer and have not reached destination.','Two more bytes accumulate, filling the chosen four-byte threshold.','flush forwards the pending bytes and clears that buffer. The threshold controls when forwarding happens.','The final single byte remains pending even though no full buffer remains to trigger the threshold.','An explicit final flush delivers that remaining byte. Forgetting it would print ABCD and lose E.']),
36:('auto private_view',4,['This value copy owns a separate string initialized to cat, modeling a private snapshot.','The & creates an alias for the existing backing string, modeling shared visibility.','Changing the private copy produces bat while leaving backing untouched.','Changing the shared alias changes backing to car. This demonstrates visibility rules but does not call mmap or model persistence.']),
37:('auto parent_offset',4,['A shared_ptr owns one dynamically allocated offset, initially zero.','Copying this handle shares the same integer and adds an owner; it does not copy the offset value.','The copied ordinary child_value changes independently, leaving parent_value equal to 7.','Dereferencing child_offset changes the shared integer to 2, visible through parent_offset too. This separates copied process values from shared open-file state.']),
38:('const int pid',3,['The fixed process identifier is 42 for this model. const prevents accidental changes through pid.','image names the current program image, initially shell.','Replacing the image with worker changes the modeled program while retaining pid. This string assignment models successful exec; it does not actually replace the running executable.']),
39:('const int exit_code',2,['Copy the available termination value before discarding the stored status. Dereferencing an empty optional would violate its precondition.','reset destroys the stored optional value and makes the handle empty. This models collecting a terminated child’s status, not a real wait system call.']),
40:('const auto eof',4,['The lambda tests two conditions: the buffer has no bytes and every writer handle is closed. It borrows both state variables by reference.','One writer closes, leaving one open writer. An empty buffer now means more data could still arrive.','The first EOF test prints false because one writer remains.','After the last writer closes, EOF becomes true if the buffer is still empty. Buffered bytes would have to drain first.']),
41:('pending = true',4,['One event sets the pending flag. A flag stores a state, not an event count.','A second event sets the same state again, preserving no extra multiplicity.','handled begins at zero to count how often this model performs handling.','The single true flag causes one handling step and is cleared. Two notifications therefore lead to handled=1. This ordinary bool is not a real signal-handler synchronization mechanism.']),
42:('for (std::string word',3,['The for loop declares a reusable word, tests stream extraction as its condition, and has no separate increment expression. Each successful extraction appends one token.','The fixture asserts exactly three tokens and a pipe token in the middle before indexing either side. Assertions are demonstration checks, not robust user-input validation.','The output names emit and count as separate pipeline stages. The complete lab validates malformed input before any command could run.']),
43:('const int a_read',4,['A takes a snapshot of counter while it is zero. This whole program is single-threaded so the illustrated interleaving is fully defined.','B takes its snapshot before either modeled write, also seeing zero.','A writes its old snapshot plus one, giving counter 1.','B writes its own old snapshot plus one, again 1. The second store replaces the first update. Real unsynchronized ordinary C++ thread writes would have undefined behavior, not a guaranteed result of 1.']),
44:('std::thread a',4,['The lambda captures the arrays by reference. Worker A writes only partial[0] and reads the first two immutable inputs.','Worker B writes a distinct array element and reads the other inputs, so the workers do not race on the same scalar location.','join waits for A to finish and establishes visibility of A’s completed writes. The referenced arrays remain alive.','Join B before combining both partial sums. Production thread startup needs cleanup if creating a later worker throws; the lab uses futures to manage this boundary.']),
45:('counter.store(a',3,['This store writes a+1 based on the earlier snapshot zero. Atomicity of the store alone does not refresh that snapshot.','The second atomic store writes b+1, also one, replacing the first result. Each store is indivisible, but the combined load/compute/store operation is not.','The defined split_result is one. Later fetch_add operations combine the read and modification atomically, so two updates produce two.']),
46:('payload = 42',2,['The producer writes a non-atomic payload before publishing readiness. Other threads must not read it without the matching synchronization.','A release store publishes true. A consumer acquire load that reads this value establishes visibility of prior producer writes, allowing its later payload read. Merely replacing the flag with an ordinary bool would create a data race.']),
47:('std::lock_guard',5,['Constructing lock_guard locks guard. Its destructor unlocks at the end of this scope, including stack unwinding.','The source balance must cover the transfer before the first update. This fixture checks ten units are available.','Debit the first balance while holding the lock. At this intermediate point the conservation rule is temporarily incomplete.','Credit the second balance before releasing the same lock. Other participating operations must use this lock too.','The assertion checks the restored total of 100 while the protected state is still locked. Locking each update separately would expose an invalid intermediate total.']),
48:('queue.push_back',4,['The producer’s item enters the queue before the modeled consumer checks it. The state survives even though there is no remembered notification.','The consumer waits only if the queue is empty. Here it is not empty, so waiting would be wrong.','The stream begins reporting wait=false. In a real concurrent program, the predicate must be checked under the same mutex used for updates.','The continuation prints the front value 7. The lab supplies an actual condition-variable wait whose predicate is rechecked on wakeup.']),
49:('if (queue.size()',3,['A full queue rejects this push before changing its state. This baseline is a single-threaded model, not a blocking queue.','When space exists, append the value. Capacity must be checked and mutation performed under one lock in a concurrent version.','Return true only after accepting the value. The lab turns this contract into a bounded blocking queue with explicit closure and draining.']),
50:('if (from > to)',2,['Swap the two IDs if necessary so every request orders them from smaller to larger. Both transfer directions then agree on an acquisition order.','Return the ordered pair by value. This function establishes an ordering model; it does not acquire locks. The lab uses scoped_lock on actual mutexes and handles the same-account case.']),
51:('const std::size_t length',3,['The first received byte states the payload length. This fixture already contains a header; a general parser must check for it before this access.','The declared length must satisfy both the application maximum and the available byte extent. A short stream read is not a complete message.','Construct owned message text from exactly the declared payload range. The lab additionally returns the consumed count so a following frame is not accidentally discarded.']),
52:('const unsigned limit',4,['Dividing the memory budget by per-connection cost gives a modeled admission limit of 32. This assumes the stated cost accounts for all relevant per-connection memory.','The fixture already has 32 active connections.','The output begins with the computed limit and selects word-form Booleans using boolalpha.','active < limit is false, so another connection is rejected. A real gate must combine this check with its count update under synchronization.']),
53:('if (result == -1)',2,['In this deliberately tagged fixture, -1 means would-block: stop draining now and keep the connection open. A real API requires examining the specific error code.','Positive results add the actual byte count to the buffer. EOF and other errors need separate handling, provided by the generalized lab.']),
54:('const double elapsed',3,['accumulate sums the three durations with a double initial value. For this serial fixture the total is fifteen milliseconds.','Divide total duration by three observations to obtain a mean of five milliseconds per request.','Convert milliseconds to seconds before dividing three requests by elapsed time: 3/0.015 = 200 per second. Overlapping request durations cannot be summed to infer real wall-clock throughput.']),
55:('for (std::size_t i',2,['The loop stores the sum of the first i+1 values at prefix[i+1]. The leading zero makes empty prefixes valid. Each value is added once during construction.','For the half-open index interval [1,4), subtract the sum before index one from the sum before index four. This returns 4+6+8=18 without rescanning the range.']),
56:('const double new_time',2,['Normalize original runtime to one. The unchanged fraction costs 0.6; the improved 0.4 fraction costs 0.4/2=0.2; total new runtime is 0.8.','Overall speedup is original time divided by new time, so 1/0.8=1.25. Doubling one part does not double the complete program.']),
57:('const bool valid',2,['Validate the header against the received extent before computing how much remains. The header fits here, leaving only two bytes.','&& short-circuits the subtraction when the first check fails. Claimed payload five exceeds the remaining two, so this input is rejected before accessing it.']),
58:('saved_guard ^=',3,['^= flips the selected bit of an ordinary unsigned integer. This legally models corruption without performing an invalid memory access.','Compare the guard against its known expected value and print detected because this selected guard changed.','The assertion verifies only this modeled detection. It does not prove all corruption would affect the guard or that prevention and detection are interchangeable.']),
59:('if (candidate.rfind',4,['rfind with position zero checks whether version= occurs at the beginning. Only an accepted candidate is swapped into live. This baseline’s prefix-only validation is intentionally weaker than a full configuration parser.','The rejected broken candidate leaves live equal to version=1, which is printed.','Replace the temporary candidate with version=2 while leaving live untouched.','The prefix test accepts this candidate and swap commits it. The lab strengthens validation to reject missing numbers and trailing junk.']),
60:('const int result',3,['stoi parses each fixed text value to an int; their sum is 42. General external input needs explicit parse failures and range checks.','to_string creates owned result text and the concatenation appends a newline. This string remains alive through the output operation.','Insertion sends the text through the output stream. The compiler and linker prepare this program; these operations are the source-level execution behavior.']),
61:('const auto work',5,['The lambda borrows readings and partial. Each worker receives its own worker index by value.','Multiplying the index by three selects the beginning of that worker’s disjoint three-element range.','The selected partial slot belongs to this worker. accumulate starts reading at the corresponding range beginning.','The continuation supplies the one-past range end and integer initial sum zero. Each worker reads exactly three live elements.','The callable definition ends. Both arrays must remain alive until the later joins finish; the capstone lab adds bounded work admission and shutdown.'])
}

